{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"sadistic-noir-bustard","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Observed\n\nTwo plan reviews of story `6b66-9378-ebb1-446c` on the same plan material (fingerprint `61a3ad8cb11e3d44`) and the same code SHA (`ee5253abfd4`) reached opposite verdicts because one finding was scored differently:\n\n| Run (REVIEW_RESULT sidecar ts) | Pass-1 chunks | Finding `fcf1d7edbaceb08b2` (G1G2, steps.py:230 docstring) | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `1793158045669017902` (unforced) | 0 of 14 resumed (fresh) | impact 1.0 → priority 1.0, threshold 0.8, decision `block`, margin 0.2, reason `high-priority+criterion-opted-in` | BLOCK |\n| `1793158412475539140` (forced, ~6 min later) | 14 of 14 resumed | impact 0.55 → priority 0.55, decision `advisory`, margin -0.25, reason `default-advisory` | PASS |\n\nSame finding id, same text, same location, validity 1.0 in both. The remaining findings (`f7fde2c04709ca036`, `f607dd457c67f9209`, dropped `f0163e444012934e0`) match in both runs, so the verdict flip is down to one impact score.\n\nThe forced run resumed every Pass-1 chunk from checkpoint, so the finding text was identical input; the impact difference therefore arises after Pass 1 (verification / impact scoring), not in finding discovery.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nA single borderline impact estimate decides whether a plan is blocked. An author who re-runs the gate on unchanged material can get a different verdict, and a BLOCK on one run reads as a plan defect that the next run does not confirm. Found while investigating `obeliskoid-indigoid-egg` (`c3c0-0b27-a2eb-4084`), where the BLOCK was first misread as a replayed stale result.\n\n## Not established\n\n- Which step produced each impact score (the verification pass output vs a later floor) — the sidecars record the final value only.\n- How often the same finding's impact varies across runs on unchanged material; this is one observed pair.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The step that assigned impact 1.0 vs 0.55 to `fcf1d7edbaceb08b2` is identified from recorded inputs/outputs or a replay.\n- [ ] Run-to-run variance of a blocking decision on unchanged material is measured on a replay set, and either bounded by a design change or documented as accepted behaviour with the measured rate.","id":"5503-c37b-2a44-447c","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["plan-review-gate","correctness"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Same finding on unchanged plan scored impact 1.0 then 0.55: BLOCK vs PASS"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793495970544309001,"uuid":"eba71707-8096-4278-b7c9-7aa2f93b1ac8"}